NOT COVERED BY THIS LICENSE

Some optional tooling in this repository depends on Ultralytics YOLO
(https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics), which is licensed under
AGPL-3.0, not Apache-2.0. AGPL-3.0 is a strong copyleft license and its terms
are not compatible with redistributing the affected parts under Apache-2.0.

These files are therefore NOT distributed with this repository:

  - model_weights/yolov11_ear_detector.pt   (a model trained with Ultralytics)
  - finetune_yolov11.py
  - utils/yolo11_demo.py

They remain usable locally but are excluded from version control, so nothing
under AGPL-3.0 is redistributed here.

Two files that ARE distributed can optionally call Ultralytics, and import it
lazily so that neither the package nor its terms are required to use them:

  - data_prep.py   (label collection; the YOLO path proposes pseudo-labels)
  - relabel.py     (the `propose` subcommand)

`ultralytics` is deliberately absent from requirements.txt. Nothing in the
BlazeEar model, its training, its evaluation, or the browser demo needs it:
it was an auto-labeller used while building data/splits/*.csv, which are not
distributed here either. Installing it to re-run label proposal means
accepting AGPL-3.0 for that use.
